  "result": "Namespaces are implemented and the full suite passes (8 tests, both files).\n\n**What I changed**\n\n- `kvstore/store.py`: the SQLite `kv` table now has an `ns` column with a composite `PRIMARY KEY (ns, key)`, so the same key can hold different values per namespace. `set`, `get`, `delete`, and `keys` take `ns: str = \"default\"` and filter on it. Added `count(ns)` using `COUNT(*)` and `namespaces()` using `SELECT DISTINCT ns ... ORDER BY ns`, which naturally returns only namespaces that currently hold at least one key.\n- **Legacy migration**: on open, if an existing file has the old `kv(key, value)` schema, it's renamed, recreated with the new schema, and all rows are moved into the `default` namespace inside one transaction. I verified this against a hand-built old-format file. New and already-migrated files are untouched. Everything still lives in the single data file.\n- `SPEC.md`: updated the public interface block and added a short note describing namespace semantics.\n\nNothing under `tests/` was modified. Note that `store.py` and `test_t2.py` are still untracked in git, as they were when I started. I did not commit since you didn't ask for that.",
